2026-09-26 — K11j: separate filter correctness from timing-model assertions.

Historical original seccomp_benchmark: both kernels have 2 PASS / 2 FAIL /
3 SKIP. Every measured getpid call returned the expected PID. The two FAILs
are source lines 284-288: approx(per_filter1, per_filter2) and the one/two
bitmap overhead comparison. approx permits ten percent or two nanoseconds.
Historical reference costs [native, bitmap1, bitmap2, filter1, filter2] are
[110,135,139,159,164] ns: per-filter estimates 5 versus 8, bitmap overheads
25 versus 29. Subject costs [158,233,222,310,345] ns give 35 versus 25 and
75 versus 64. These are the exact failed arithmetic comparisons, not syscall
value mismatches. The remaining three SKIPs follow the failed bitmap-cost
comparison; they do not independently establish missing bitmap support.

Permanent C reduction uses the original two filter forms and installation
sequence. Each stage checks 1024 real syscall return values, not a simulated
filter. It additionally rejects an out-of-bounds filter load, then installs
getpid->EPERM and verifies that previous ALLOW filters cannot bypass it while
getppid remains allowed. GCC14 and Clang19 static O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
ELFs each pass 14 assertions on each retained kernel: 28 PASS per Image.
Both diagnostic boots and normal shutdowns PASS. This is not a concurrency,
all-seccomp, bitmap-internals or complete security validation claim.

Unchanged originals subsequently run once per Image on the historical HVF
host/4-CPU/2-GiB lane with the original 180-second limit and no sample argument:
  reference: 7 PASS / 0 FAIL / 0 SKIP; [108,133,133,153,161] ns;
             normal shutdown at guest uptime 93.535173 s.
  subject:   7 PASS / 0 FAIL / 0 SKIP; [155,212,212,305,334] ns;
             normal shutdown at guest uptime 115.702473 s.
No kernel/compiler/test/tolerance was changed. The source itself calls this a
relative-performance benchmark; seccomp_run_filters promises action selection,
not a linear/stable nanosecond cost. This closes classification of the observed
failures as timing-model assertions. It does NOT establish a compiler repair,
identify the physical cause of every timing variation, erase the historical
FAILs, or guarantee the final K13 replay. The measured subject slowdown remains.

Preparation: existing sealed ARM64 image, network none, GCC 14.2.0-19 and
Clang 19.1.7; build.sh compiles the two ELF controls and reuses selftest-init.
Execution: existing tools/k1/selftest.py.flight with snapshot=on. Tiny payload
2201600 bytes; existing 64 MiB scratch and retained matched full runtime disks
are hash-checked unchanged. No new runtime disk or kernel clone.
Capture/scripts: .build/floating-targeted/seccomp-chain-20260926/
  build.sh; replay.py; replay.py --original
gate-changed bddac04 selects no Rust crate for this standalone diagnostic;
renderer, JSON and diff checks PASS. No new Rust/workspace gate is claimed.

